  "semantics": [
    "Raw self resolves through PTKNOWN to the exact defining class, before ordinary imports; changing the consumer namespace cannot rebind that class.",
    "Existing nullable recursion and eight ordered two-member class/builtin laws reuse the same proof, retaining complete raw and normalized order and source metadata.",
    "Distinct same-class seed and replacement objects retain their own uninitialized backing slots. Actual reference aliases, ordinary object copies, atomic refused writes and real per-object type-source detachment use existing runtime and ownership rules.",
    "The free empty array literal retains its authenticated constant-pool owners after runtime aliases retire. The initial overstrong draft retirement expectation was corrected before any state interpreter run.",
    "Four original-source agreements cover self, nullable self and the two self/int member orders under weak and strict callers. All eight builtin pair alternatives have separate header132 coverage; source4 does not independently validate all eight builtin runtime tags.",
    "Known-scope self intersections are valid at the target. Unchanged nominal-shape helpers leave larger self unions/intersections/DNF outside this hook admission; no new PHP static-error claim is made."
  ],
